      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Crossed renal ectopia is a rare urinary tract anomaly, often associated with malformations involving various organs and systems. We report a case of crossed renal ectopy with fusion, without associated abnormalities. Recurrent abdominal pain, sometimes with microhematuria, were the clinical features, never accompanied by alteration of the renal function."},
